proof.text:
Fix $e:S\hookrightarrow T$ equal to $i$ or $j$. Let $C$ be a complex of etale $A$-module sheaves on $S$. Apply [lem-cbc-proetale-extension-zero-comparison] in each degree, obtaining $a_C^r:
u_T^*e_!^{\mathrm{et}}C^r\xrightarrow{\sim}e_!^{\mathrm{proet}}
u_S^*C^r$. Naturality of that sheaf comparison gives $(e_!^{\mathrm{proet}}
u_S^*d_C^r)a_C^r=a_C^{r+1}(
u_T^*e_!^{\mathrm{et}}d_C^r)$. Thus $a_C$ and its componentwise inverse are inverse chain maps, natural in chain maps. The two composites invert quasi-isomorphisms by steps 1--3. Part (2) of [lem-weil-pbc-localization-universal-property] therefore gives a natural isomorphism $\delta_e$ on the derived categories whose component on $QC$ is the image of $a_C$ under localization, with the factorization identifications. Uniqueness and part (3) of that lemma show independence from the representative. Restrict to $D^+$ by step 3. This constructs both displayed $\delta$ maps with precisely their prescribed normalization. Use the identical construction with openImmersionLowerShriekComparisonUpperStarIso for j and i; both normalization equalities are reflexivity.
